{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"\"This is working now\" — merge the current feature branch into the repo's default branch (local master, else main) and push it upstream, then return to the feature branch. Transactional: requires that you are ON the branch being merged, no conflicts, no merge in flight; checkout default → merge --no-ff → push origin <default> → checkout back, bailing with the step's stderr on any failure. A dirty tree is NOT a blocker: git itself refuses a checkout or merge that would overwrite an edit (gitrun reports the refusal verbatim and the command steps back to the branch with nothing changed), and edits it does not touch ride along untouched, reported as `carried` (Cargo.lock, rewritten by every build, is the standing case). A real merge conflict is reported with the tree left mid-merge on the default branch (resolve then commit, or dev.git merge --abort) — never silently half-merged. Returns {status, msg, branch, default, carried, steps}.","import":"use ndata::dataarray::DataArray;","params":[{"name":"repo","type":"String"},{"name":"branch","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"rwuprt1a05cfd1d26o118","readers":[],"time":1788647665371,"username":"system","writers":[]}